WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en-RO

00:00:05.859 --> 00:00:07.859
Hello and welcome back to Lam Rim (LAM RIM).

00:00:08.320 --> 00:00:11.080
We begin episode no.  9. I like

00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:13.320
to call it
"A visit in the middle of the sun."  We

00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:20.900
talked about
something that is big enough and strong enough.

00:00:21.420 --> 00:00:29.380
It's like a nuclear bomb used to clean ketchup
off your shirt or something.

00:00:31.029 --> 00:00:35.879
And I'm not exaggerating.
I want you to think like that.

00:00:36.790 --> 00:00:38.410
Imagine...

00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:43.240
Today is Independence Day in America.
I'm talking about Independence Day.  We

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:53.600
often go on picnics with our family.
It's the middle of summer.

00:00:54.520 --> 00:01:02.880
And American kids will eat hot dogs
or hamburgers and put too much ketchup on them,
and a little drop of ketchup will jump out here.

00:01:04.680 --> 00:01:13.200
Imagine that to clean it, mom sends the shirt or blouse into the middle of the sun

00:01:13.200 --> 00:01:16.420
[Inaudible]

00:01:16.420 --> 00:01:20.840
To clean a small drop of ketchup, of red ketchup.

00:01:23.220 --> 00:01:25.380
I know it seems like a strange image,

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:31.020
but I want you to try to think about it.  I want you to
try to think about it.  I don't

00:01:31.020 --> 00:01:33.060
know what we could compare it to.  I don't

00:01:37.500 --> 00:01:41.980
know.
Just put something small in the middle of the sun, okay?

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:46.120
So we're going to visit the middle of the sun today.

00:01:46.340 --> 00:01:55.280
And I'm happy to announce that we've just reached the third and final section of the lam rim.  The

00:01:55.460 --> 00:01:57.360
Stepwise Path to Enlightenment.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:04.700
Now we are about to move
into the activities of a bodhisattva.

00:02:05.080 --> 00:02:12.040
We are about to move to the
way of thinking and acting of a bodhisattva,

00:02:12.040 --> 00:02:16.260
who is the person with the highest goal.
@KYES BU CHEN PO

00:02:16.260 --> 00:02:19.700
Which means a person with high purpose.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:26.280
Those of you, especially those who have participated in this lam rim for the past ten years,

00:02:26.680 --> 00:02:33.860
should be very happy that you survived
and that I survived to reach the last part.  We've

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:37.580
reached the last part.  It
's the last third.

00:02:38.920 --> 00:02:43.360
Now, the mathematicians among you should calculate logically:

00:02:44.079 --> 00:02:46.529
Geshe-la, you just said that we still have 25% to make of this lam rim.

00:02:48.220 --> 00:02:51.240
So where does this last third come from?

00:02:51.240 --> 00:03:02.500
And the answer is that the treatment
prescribed by Pabongka Rinpoche for the last two days
of the lam rim is too short.

00:03:03.180 --> 00:03:09.540
His presentation on meditation
and the perception of emptiness,

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:14.480
which are the last two perfections of the six,
is not very long.

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.680
And I don't know what happened.  I mean
, sometimes-- it

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:23.820
's like the sponsor comes to him and says we're going to run out of food in two days.

00:03:23.820 --> 00:03:24.860
Let's finish!

00:03:24.860 --> 00:03:31.140
It's possible it's
a mystical message from Tara.

00:03:31.180 --> 00:03:35.960
Maybe, I don't know,
maybe he had another meeting in another city.

00:03:38.080 --> 00:03:50.480
But if you ask me, Pabongka Rinpoche
made the last two parts shorter because
Je Tsongkhapa included them in his great Lam Rim.

00:03:50.520 --> 00:03:54.600
"The Great Book
of the Stages of the Path to Enlightenment,"
Lam Rim Chenmo

00:03:55.160 --> 00:04:01.040
Tsongkhapa did such a good job that I think I
can see Pabongka Rinpoche saying,

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.540
"You see, I don't
have much reason to teach this part

00:04:06.420 --> 00:04:12.560
because Tsongkhapa has already taught it
and done it in a tremendous way."

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:17.940
There are many, many stories about
Tsongkhapa who wrote these last two parts,

00:04:18.700 --> 00:04:21.780
and I am very happy
because we will study them together.

00:04:21.780 --> 00:04:29.260
So we will end this lam rim series
with amazing teachings on meditation and emptiness.

00:04:29.880 --> 00:04:38.680
And that's why this part about the stages of the path for people who have bodhichitta,

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:40.440
for Bodhisattvas,

00:04:40.640 --> 00:04:44.020
is not as long as it could have been.

00:04:44.280 --> 00:04:46.640
So let's get started.
Let's read the Tibetan:

00:04:47.200 --> 00:04:50.780
@ GSUM PA SKYES BU CHEN PO'I LAM GYI RIM
PAR BLO SBYANG BA LA

00:04:51.340 --> 00:04:57.820
Let's train our hearts on the path to enlightenment
for highly motivated people --

00:04:58.140 --> 00:05:00.520
people who are bodhisattvas.

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:04.700
@THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO SEMS BSKYED KHO NAR BSTAN PA PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA

00:05:04.700 --> 00:05:09.500
He says we will walk through this
way of life of a bodhisattva.  we

00:05:09.500 --> 00:05:11.560
will go through it in three different stages.

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:13.440
Number one.

00:05:14.040 --> 00:05:19.860
@ THEG CHEN GYI 'JUG SGO
If you wish to enter the path of a bodhisattva,
there is only one way to get there.

00:05:20.520 --> 00:05:23.620
And this is by achieving a certain mental state.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:29.660
If you want to become enlightened,
if you want to have a chance to become enlightened,

00:05:30.160 --> 00:05:36.260
if you want to have a chance to help the world,
there is only one way: you
must attain bodhichitta.

00:05:36.260 --> 00:05:44.460
You must obtain this desire to attain enlightenment
so that you can help countless beings.

00:05:44.780 --> 00:05:47.700
Now, I want to talk about what countless means.

00:05:48.400 --> 00:05:53.500
Bodhichitta aims at countless living beings.  It

00:05:53.500 --> 00:06:00.540
doesn't target all the people in your city or all the people in your country or all the people on this planet.

00:06:00.540 --> 00:06:01.920
Expand!

00:06:02.240 --> 00:06:06.800
If we want to send the virus to the middle of the Sun,
if we want to visit the middle of the Sun, we

00:06:06.800 --> 00:06:14.220
have to give up this idea that we are working
[only] for all the people on this planet.
We don't do that.

00:06:14.760 --> 00:06:23.680
Give up this idea that we're trying to help
all the fish and all the birds and all the
land animals.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:24.840
We don't do that.  That's not the point

00:06:24.840 --> 00:06:26.620
.

00:06:27.460 --> 00:06:30.560
We encompass the entire universe.

00:06:30.560 --> 00:06:39.300
We [each] decide today, that I would like to help
every living creature in the universe.

00:06:39.500 --> 00:06:42.540
Every little virus.

00:06:42.540 --> 00:06:44.360
Bacteria.

00:06:45.300 --> 00:06:47.300
Every whale.

00:06:48.040 --> 00:06:51.640
Every human in the universe.

00:06:51.640 --> 00:06:58.980
Going out at night in Sedona or outside of Sedona,
in Rim Rock is better.

00:06:58.980 --> 00:07:03.340
And look at the stars and try to imagine.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:20.640
First of all, you cannot practice the way of life of a bodhisattva
if you do not expand your mind towards this goal.

00:07:23.360 --> 00:07:28.709
And if you really experience this fact,
-- which takes some practice,

00:07:28.709 --> 00:07:30.850
if you really send your mind --

00:07:30.850 --> 00:07:41.480
if you're really able to attain bodhichitta,
then the things you have to do in this world are nothing.  It does

00:07:41.480 --> 00:07:44.780
n't mean anything.  It's something insignificant.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:51.380
Helping all the people in this world means nothing.  It's
easy.

00:07:53.620 --> 00:07:59.640
@PHAN YON DANG BCAS PA means
I want to tell you the benefits of such thinking.
This is the first stage.

00:07:59.640 --> 00:08:02.657
@BYANG CHUB TU SEMS BSKYED PA'I TSUL
Second stage.

00:08:02.660 --> 00:08:06.560
How do you reach this achievement?
Mental achievement?

00:08:06.560 --> 00:08:11.180
How do you perceive the entire universe
and all beings in it?

00:08:11.180 --> 00:08:15.800
And then develop love for them?
Is it possible?

00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.760
Is it possible?
This is the second stage.

00:08:19.760 --> 00:08:23.560
Third stage.
@SEMS BSKYED NAS SPYOD PA LA SLOB TSUL LO

00:08:24.140 --> 00:08:27.080
We will learn how to behave like a bodhisattva.

00:08:27.400 --> 00:08:34.900
Once I have this aspiration to become a bodhisattva
what should I actually do?

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:41.300
How do I spend my daytime hours
if I want to act like a bodhisattva?

00:08:41.300 --> 00:08:43.260
What to do?

00:08:43.740 --> 00:08:48.600
What will my schedule be?  All

00:08:49.260 --> 00:08:51.200
right.  This is the first oath.

00:08:51.780 --> 00:08:58.860
@) DANG PO NI,
DE LTAR SKYES BU CHUNG 'BRING GI SKABS SU NGES 'BYUNG GI BSAM PAS KUN NAS BSLANGS

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:08.340
Now that we have gone through the steps on the path of people with low motivation and with average motivation,

00:09:08.340 --> 00:09:13.960
at least you should have this feeling that

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.100
indeed this life is pain, indeed this life means problems.

00:09:17.100 --> 00:09:20.580
The virus is just a way of emphasizing the obvious.

00:09:21.060 --> 00:09:23.020
But it's always been like this.  There has

00:09:23.020 --> 00:09:25.940
always been a virus called death.

00:09:25.940 --> 00:09:29.280
This virus is the new one.  It's much smaller.

00:09:30.720 --> 00:09:33.340
But at least now we're all thinking about him.

00:09:34.080 --> 00:09:37.220
@ LHAG PA'I BSLAB PA GSUM LA 'BAD PAS

00:09:37.640 --> 00:09:42.479
Then we should
work on the three extraordinary workouts.

00:09:42.480 --> 00:09:44.580
Treat others well.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.720
Spend time in meditation.

00:09:48.510 --> 00:09:52.980
And then try to see
that things don't come by themselves.

00:09:53.020 --> 00:09:59.540
@'BAD PAS RANG GCIG PUS
THAR BA'I GO 'PHANG
THOB TZAM DANG 'KHOR BA
LAS LDOG TZAM 'BYUNG

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:02.960
You can reach nirvana alone

00:10:03.400 --> 00:10:06.980
and get out of the Wheel of Life.

00:10:07.380 --> 00:10:11.500
If you practice these attitudes then you can, it is possible.

00:10:11.820 --> 00:10:14.000
But I've learned that already, I'm done with it.

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:16.000
@ DE TZAM GYIS MI CHOG

00:10:16.460 --> 00:10:18.347
But I don't want you to stop here.  I do

00:10:18.347 --> 00:10:20.880
n't want you to stop here.  I want you

00:10:20.880 --> 00:10:25.040
to take care of much more important things.  There

00:10:25.520 --> 00:10:30.980
are much more important things to do.  Don't stop here.

00:10:30.980 --> 00:10:33.680
@SPANG BYA THAMS CAD MA SPANGS

00:10:35.340 --> 00:10:39.500
If you stick to what I have taught you so far,

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:43.260
you will not cleanse your heart

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:45.560
of all the unclean things there.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:50.240
@ THOB BYA YON TAN
THAMS CAD KYANG YONGS SU MA RDZOGS PAS

00:10:50.240 --> 00:10:51.560
and you would not attain

00:10:51.560 --> 00:10:54.120
the highest
spiritual qualities you could attain.

00:10:54.680 --> 00:10:56.680
@ MA RDZOGS PAS
Therefore,

00:10:56.840 --> 00:11:02.480
@ RANG DON DANG,
GZHAN DON YANG NYI TSE BA LAS MI 'BYUNG

00:11:02.780 --> 00:11:08.320
@NYI TSE BA is a very discouraging word here.

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:11.600
It's a very sad word here.

00:11:11.880 --> 00:11:16.340
It is said that, you can work with these methods that I have taught you so far,

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.480
you can work with
all those meditations that I have taught you so far,

00:11:20.100 --> 00:11:25.120
but the amount of good
that you will do for yourself and for others

00:11:25.120 --> 00:11:29.040
is only a small amount of what you need to do.

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:34.900
@ NYI TSE BA means it's just a small amount
of what you should be doing.

00:11:36.400 --> 00:11:43.520
And by the way, the most common use of this word is the Tibetan word for hell on earth.

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:45.900
Which is very strange.

00:11:45.900 --> 00:11:49.580
So, it's a big hell where people can go.

00:11:50.060 --> 00:11:56.840
But I always think of a person who had a car accident and the car exploded and burst into flames.

00:11:58.340 --> 00:12:02.945
In the scriptures this is called
@NYI TSI BA'I DMYAL BA

00:12:02.945 --> 00:12:08.220
A little piece of hell on this plane.  In this plane of reality.

00:12:08.920 --> 00:12:13.080
And so this word @NYI TSI BA means just a small piece.

00:12:13.080 --> 00:12:17.780
And here he says, do you want to help yourself
and help other people too?

00:12:18.620 --> 00:12:22.420
All I've taught you so far for 10 years is
@NYI STI BA.

00:12:22.560 --> 00:12:30.160
That's just a small part of what you could do, and now we're ready to start the serious stuff.

00:12:30.160 --> 00:12:35.880
Well Geshe-la, why did I spend 10 years doing @NYI TSI BA, the small things?

00:12:36.640 --> 00:12:39.460
Why didn't we go on to bigger things?

00:12:40.020 --> 00:12:44.660
Because small things are a ladder
that helps you reach great things.  You ca

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:50.080
n't achieve great things
if you don't do the other two parts.

00:12:50.080 --> 00:12:55.093
If you don't practice all the steps in the lam rim
in their correct order you will

00:12:55.093 --> 00:12:58.460
never reach the part with the bodhisattva.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.560
So, you can't say I don't want to.

00:13:02.560 --> 00:13:10.260
Part of the bodhisattva way of life is mastering the lower path that helped you get here.

00:13:10.720 --> 00:13:14.760
And never reject it.
You just have to grow out of it.

00:13:15.380 --> 00:13:21.140
@MI 'BYUNG ZHING SLAR THEG CHEN
LA GZHI NAS 'JUG DGOS LA

00:13:22.860 --> 00:13:27.320
This is an idea in Buddhism,

00:13:27.960 --> 00:13:30.320
that as soon as you're ready

00:13:30.320 --> 00:13:32.460
and as soon as you've gone through the path of preparation, you

00:13:33.200 --> 00:13:37.300
should go straight to the
way of life of a Bodhisattva

00:13:37.980 --> 00:13:42.080
because if you don't, you
'll have to do it again anyway, so

00:13:42.080 --> 00:13:44.749
sooner or later, you'll have to get here.

00:13:45.440 --> 00:13:49.700
This life may last.
Or it may be later in this life.

00:13:50.500 --> 00:13:57.780
People come to me from time to time and say, "I'm going to take a break from this dharma.

00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:01.960
I feel like I need to take a break.

00:14:02.380 --> 00:14:05.740
I have other things to do right now.

00:14:05.740 --> 00:14:10.600
I have a big project at work
or I have some family situations

00:14:11.220 --> 00:14:15.600
and I need to take a break."

00:14:15.600 --> 00:14:19.400
I remember once in India, I said to one of my teachers,

00:14:23.370 --> 00:14:25.350
45 years ago,

00:14:25.350 --> 00:14:31.960
I said, "I need to take a break," and he looked at me and said, "Yeah, okay, but you'll come back. You'll come

00:14:32.220 --> 00:14:36.120
back because you have nowhere else to go. You'll come back

00:14:36.540 --> 00:14:44.300
. You'll come back to this because you need to come back to this. Life will bring you back here."

00:14:45.029 --> 00:14:47.929
Because that's life.  You need a lam rim.

00:14:48.860 --> 00:14:52.901
Life will always bring you back to lam rim.
Unless you die.

00:14:52.901 --> 00:14:55.680
And even so, it will bring you back later.

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.600
@ SLAR means you have to go back.
@ SLAR THEG CHEN LA GZHI NAS

00:15:02.600 --> 00:15:07.250
@ GZHI NAS means you will waste a lot of time
if you have to go back.

00:15:07.250 --> 00:15:12.780
